+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Ensures registered Flask teardown cleanup is completed despite individual cleanup failures.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Complete teardown execution after failures
+During request and application-context teardown, Flask MUST attempt every registered teardown callback and the corresponding teardown signal even when one or more earlier callbacks or receivers raise an exception.
+
+#### Scenario: Request teardown callback raises
+- **WHEN** a request teardown callback raises before other callbacks and request teardown signal receivers run
+- **THEN** Flask attempts all remaining request teardown callbacks and signal receivers before raising the cleanup failure
+
+#### Scenario: Application-context teardown callback raises
+- **WHEN** an application-context teardown callback raises before other callbacks and application-context teardown signal receivers run
+- **THEN** Flask attempts all remaining application-context teardown callbacks and signal receivers before raising the cleanup failure
+
+### Requirement: Report collected teardown failures after cleanup
+Flask MUST raise teardown failures only after all teardown callbacks and the teardown signal have been attempted. On Python versions supporting exception groups, the raised exception MUST preserve every collected teardown failure; otherwise Flask MUST raise at least the first collected teardown failure.
+
+#### Scenario: Multiple teardown failures occur
+- **WHEN** multiple teardown callbacks or signal receivers raise during one teardown operation
+- **THEN** the error raised after cleanup preserves all failures on a Python version that supports exception groups
+
+### Requirement: Restore context-local state before teardown errors escape
+Flask MUST restore context-local state before a teardown failure raised during context exit is exposed to the caller.
+
+#### Scenario: Context exit raises a teardown failure
+- **WHEN** context exit encounters one or more teardown failures
+- **THEN** the caller observes no active request or application context after catching the teardown error
